  "as_of_notes": "Figures are TOTAL ACTIVE REGISTRATION (active voters only) from the Maryland Board of Elections Voter Registration Activity Report for May 2026, an end-of-month snapshot dated as of 2026-05-31. The report's TOTAL row also lists 249,712 statewide INACTIVE voters (not included here). Counts are unofficial/preliminary per MD SBE convention until certified. 24 jurisdictions = 23 counties + Baltimore City (independent city, FIPS 24510). Baltimore County is FIPS 24005 and is distinct.",
  "data_quality": "high",
  "notes": "Source is the official Maryland State Board of Elections monthly PDF; latest available is May 2026. All 24 jurisdiction rows and all party columns independently re-summed and reconcile exactly to the printed TOTAL row (active total 4,323,311). Maryland's recognized parties in this report are Democratic (DEM), Republican (REP), Green (GRN), and Working Class Party (WCP); there is NO Libertarian party column. To fit the requested schema, 'Green' maps to GRN; 'Libertarian' is set to 0 because Maryland does not separately report Libertarian (Libertarian registrants are subsumed within the state's 'Other' category); 'Other' here = OTH (70,534 statewide) + WCP/Working Class Party (4,874 statewide) so that by_party sums equal each total. 'Unaffiliated' maps to UNA. Statewide active by original MD columns: DEM 2,217,757; REP 1,019,362; GRN 6,171; WCP 4,874; UNA 1,004,613; OTH 70,534; TOTAL 4,323,311."
